Subject: [PATCH] networking: respect wrapped regex attribute lookup

Streamlink 8.6.1 wraps urllib3.util.url._PERCENT_RE and forwards regex
methods through __getattr__. If Streamlink is imported before yt-dlp,
Urllib3PercentREOverride wraps that object instead of a re.Pattern.

Calling __getattribute__ directly bypasses Streamlink's __getattr__.
urllib3 >= 2.8.0 then fails when normalizing a hostname with _PERCENT_RE.sub,
breaking requests for every plugin in the same Python process.

Use normal attribute lookup so the wrapped object's forwarding is honored.
The subn override that preserves percent-encoding case remains unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/yt_dlp/networking/_requests.py
+++ b/yt_dlp/networking/_requests.py
@@ -89,7 +89,7 @@ class Urllib3PercentREOverride:
 
     # pass through all other attribute calls to the original re
     def __getattr__(self, item):
-        return self.re.__getattribute__(item)
+        return getattr(self.re, item)
 
     def subn(self, repl, string, *args, **kwargs):
         return string, self.re.subn(repl, string, *args, **kwargs)[1]
